The '''2026 Melbourne FIA Formula 2 round''' was a motor racing event held between 6 and 8 March 2026 at the [[Albert Park Circuit]]. It served as the opening round of the [[2026 Formula 2 Championship|2026 FIA Formula 2 Championship]] and was held in support of the [[2026 Australian Grand Prix]].

== Classification ==

=== Practice ===
[[Gabriele Minì]] of [[MP Motorsport]] set the fastest lap of the free practice session on Friday. Two red flags were issued during practice; [[Hitech Grand Prix|Hitech]]'s [[Colton Herta]] crashed midway through his first session at a [[Formula One race weekend|Formula One Grand Prix weekend]], and an off-track excursion by Formula 2 debutant [[Tasanapol Inthraphuvasak]] eventually ended the session prematurely.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=6 March 2026 |title=Mini leads Leon in F2’s Melbourne practice as Herta crashes |url=https://formulascout.com/mini-leads-leon-in-f2s-melbourne-practice-as-herta-crashes/138511 |access-date=7 March 2026 |website=Formula Scout }}</ref>

